WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.790
<v Examiner>Making sperm and eggs.

2
00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:03.479
<v Examiner>Four marks.

3
00:00:03.929 --> 00:00:07.896
<v Examiner>Describe the gamete production process in males and in females.

4
00:00:07.896 --> 00:00:10.415
<v Examiner>What hormone from the brain drives this?

5
00:00:10.865 --> 00:00:11.450
The hook.

6
00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:15.350
Sperm start at puberty, never stop, and one cell makes four.

7
00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:20.484
Eggs start before birth, pause, go one a month, finish only if a sperm gets in,

8
00:00:20.484 --> 00:00:21.979
and one cell makes one.

9
00:00:22.429 --> 00:00:24.436
Males first: spermatogenesis.

10
00:00:24.436 --> 00:00:30.249
It happens in the seminiferous tubules of the testes, continuously, from puberty on.

11
00:00:30.249 --> 00:00:34.332
Spermatogonia divide by mitosis into primary spermatocytes.

12
00:00:34.332 --> 00:00:37.238
Meiosis one gives secondary spermatocytes.

13
00:00:37.238 --> 00:00:39.245
Meiosis two gives spermatids.

14
00:00:39.245 --> 00:00:44.573
Then comes spermiogenesis: they lose most of their cytoplasm and grow a tail.

15
00:00:44.573 --> 00:00:47.133
One primary spermatocyte, four sperm.

16
00:00:48.583 --> 00:00:49.812
Females: oogenesis.

17
00:00:49.812 --> 00:00:51.364
It starts in fetal life.

18
00:00:51.364 --> 00:00:56.990
Oogonia divide by mitosis into primary oocytes, which begin meiosis one, and then stop,

19
00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.577
arrested in prophase one, until puberty.

20
00:00:59.577 --> 00:01:02.487
There are about two million of them at birth.

21
00:01:02.487 --> 00:01:06.691
From puberty, each month one primary oocyte finishes meiosis one,

22
00:01:06.691 --> 00:01:09.989
giving a secondary oocyte and the first polar body.

23
00:01:09.989 --> 00:01:15.292
The secondary oocyte arrests again, in metaphase two, and that's what is ovulated.

24
00:01:15.292 --> 00:01:18.590
Meiosis two is only completed if a sperm enters it,

25
00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:21.177
giving one ovum and a second polar body.

26
00:01:21.177 --> 00:01:23.570
And egg production ends at menopause.

27
00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:29.574
The hormone: FSH, follicle-stimulating hormone, from the anterior pituitary,

28
00:01:29.574 --> 00:01:31.401
working together with LH.

29
00:01:32.851 --> 00:01:33.555
The traps.

30
00:01:33.555 --> 00:01:36.512
One primary spermatocyte makes four sperm.

31
00:01:36.512 --> 00:01:41.088
One primary oocyte makes only one egg; the rest are polar bodies.

32
00:01:41.088 --> 00:01:45.312
Second: eggs start before birth, and sperm start at puberty.

33
00:01:45.312 --> 00:01:49.747
Third: the egg only finishes meiosis two after a sperm gets in.

34
00:01:50.197 --> 00:01:50.771
<v Examiner>Once more.

35
00:01:50.771 --> 00:01:52.032
<v Examiner>Making sperm and eggs.

36
00:01:54.482 --> 00:01:59.739
Spermatogenesis happens in the seminiferous tubules, continuously from puberty.

37
00:01:59.739 --> 00:02:03.665
Spermatogonia divide by mitosis into primary spermatocytes,

38
00:02:03.665 --> 00:02:08.057
then meiosis one and two give spermatids, which become four sperm.

39
00:02:08.057 --> 00:02:13.713
Oogenesis starts in fetal life: primary oocytes arrest in prophase one until puberty.

40
00:02:13.713 --> 00:02:17.972
From puberty, one a month completes meiosis one and is ovulated,

41
00:02:17.972 --> 00:02:22.297
and meiosis two finishes only if a sperm enters, giving one ovum.

42
00:02:22.297 --> 00:02:26.290
Both are driven by FSH from the anterior pituitary, with LH.
